\f5\b\fs32 \cf0 \outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec6 Joan Mir\'f3\'92s 1971 
\f6\i \ul \strokec6 Le L\'e9zard aux plumes d'or
\f5\i0 \ulnone \strokec6  (The Lizard with Golden Feathers)
\f0\b0  is a masterpiece of the 
\f4\i \strokec6 livre d\'92artiste
\f0\i0 \strokec6  (artist's book) movement, where text, image, and physical book design fuse into a single, unbreakable artwork. Featured in the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.mfa.org/exhibition/picasso-miro-dali-unbound"}}{\fldrslt \cf7 \ul \ulc7 \strokec7 Museum of Fine Arts, Boston}} exhibition, 
\f4\i \strokec6 Picasso, Mir\'f3, Dal\'ed: Unbound
\f0\i0 \strokec6 , this exceptional object\'97bound in the publisher's vellum\'97was generously donated as a 
\f5\b Gift of Boris Fridman
\f0\b0 , a collector renowned for preserving landmark 20th-century avant-garde publications. [{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.mfa.org/exhibition/picasso-miro-dali-unbound"}}{\fldrslt \cf7 \ul \ulc7 \strokec7 1}}, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.bonart.cat/en/n/47016/picasso-miro-and-dali-reinvent-the-book-as-a-work-of-art-at-the-mfa-in-boston"}}{\fldrslt \cf7 \ul \ulc7 \strokec7 2}}, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.mfa.org/exhibition/picasso-miro-dali-unbound"}}{\fldrslt \cf7 \ul \ulc7 \strokec7 3}}]\
Visitors looking at this work can be told a compelling three-part story about it:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\fs28 \cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f5\b\fs40 \cf0 1. The Artist as Poet: A Surreal Fable\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\ls4\ilvl0
\fs32 \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec6 A Complete Vision:
\f0\b0  Unlike typical illustrated books where an artist interprets someone else's writing, Mir\'f3 authored both the surrealist poetic text and the visuals himself. [{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://choicecontemporary.com/collections/joan-miro-le-lezard-aux-plumes-dor?srsltid=AfmBOoqkQ77RqAWSO3c6TDHIHBVe54viQ3NYDqK05sLJDrbKROGzDX87"}}{\fldrslt \cf7 \ul \ulc7 \strokec7 1}}, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.parkwestgallery.com/blog/joan-miro-broder-collection/"}}{\fldrslt \cf7 \ul \ulc7 \strokec7 2}}, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.mfa.org/exhibition/picasso-miro-dali-unbound"}}{\fldrslt \cf7 \ul \ulc7 \strokec7 3}}]\
\ls4\ilvl0
\f5\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec6 The Cosmic Lizard:
\f0\b0  The book unfolds like an abstract, mythic fable. A symbolic lizard journeys through an imaginative dreamscape of biomorphic forms, shooting stars, and celestial signs. [{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://choicecontemporary.com/collections/joan-miro-le-lezard-aux-plumes-dor?srsltid=AfmBOoqkQ77RqAWSO3c6TDHIHBVe54viQ3NYDqK05sLJDrbKROGzDX87"}}{\fldrslt \cf7 \ul \ulc7 \strokec7 1}}, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.mfa.org/exhibition/picasso-miro-dali-unbound"}}{\fldrslt \cf7 \ul \ulc7 \strokec7 2}}, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.mfa.org/exhibition/picasso-miro-dali-unbound"}}{\fldrslt \cf7 \ul \ulc7 \strokec7 3}}]\
\ls4\ilvl0
\f5\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec6 Visual Handwriting:
\f0\b0  Mir\'f3 did not use a standard printing typeface for the text. He wrote out the poems by hand directly onto the lithographic plates, ensuring his literary voice and painterly style were visually indistinguishable. [{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.parkwestgallery.com/blog/joan-miro-broder-collection/"}}{\fldrslt \cf7 \ul \ulc7 \strokec7 1}}]\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\fs28 \cf0 \strokec6 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f5\b\fs40 \cf0 2. The Power of Print: Mourlot and Broder\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\ls5\ilvl0
\fs32 \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec6 Technical Exploitation:
\f0\b0  Published by the visionary 
\f5\b Louis Broder
\f0\b0  and printed at the legendary Parisian workshop 
\f5\b Mourlot Fr\'e8res
\f0\b0 , the project pushed lithography to its absolute limits. [{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.mfa.org/exhibition/picasso-miro-dali-unbound"}}{\fldrslt \cf7 \ul \ulc7 \strokec7 1}}, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nationalgalleries.org/art-and-artists/113686"}}{\fldrslt \cf7 \ul \ulc7 \strokec7 2}}]\
